# QUARANTINED — real parser gaps blocked on descent-level Unicode work
# (tracked in core/TODO-CORE-PARSING.md, 2026-07-16). The generated guards
# classify ALL high bytes as identifier-start (so Greek names work but
# `|→arrow` wrongly parses as an element), and COL counts bytes, not
# characters. These cases encode CORE's actual XID_Start/XID_Continue and
# char-column semantics; the `.disabled` extension keeps them out of the
# harness (which globs *.yaml) until descent decodes UTF-8 in its charclass
# and column machinery. Re-enable by renaming to .yaml — they should then
# go green with no edits.

- id: ascii_control_for_multibyte_column_tracking
  desc: ASCII control for multibyte_name_column_tracking (same shape, same events)
  udon: "|aX |b\n     c\n"
  events:
    - ElementStart
    - [Name, "aX"]
    - ElementStart
    - [Name, "b"]
    - [Text, "c"]
    - ElementEnd
    - ElementEnd

# ===========================================================================
# Content-base bookkeeping across child elements (CORE "Automatic Prose
# Dedentation"). Mined from indentation_edge_cases.yaml — these were
# regression cases for a real pre-0.8 bug (base lost when a child closed).
# ===========================================================================

# ⚠ CORE does not state whether columns count characters or bytes; the
# review's defect #6 (REVIEW-JULY-2026 §4, verified) ruled char-correct
# column tracking, and the legacy pair encoded that. Encoded here as
# CHAR-counted: 'é' is one column, so |b's pipe is at column 4 and the
# 5-space prose line (column 5 > 4) is INSIDE |b. A byte-counting parser
# would put |b at column 5 and dedent the prose out of it — that divergence
# is exactly what this case pins. Spec-text gap worth a SPEC-CORE note.
- id: multibyte_name_column_tracking
  desc: columns count characters, not bytes — prose one past a multibyte-named line's inline child stays inside it
  udon: "|aé |b\n     c\n"
  events:
    - ElementStart
    - [Name, "aé"]
    - ElementStart
    - [Name, "b"]
    - [Text, "c"]
    - ElementEnd
    - ElementEnd

- id: symbol_start_is_prose
  desc: a non-identifier symbol after the pipe fails the element guard — prose
  udon: "|→arrow\n"
  events:
    - [Text, "|→arrow"]
